import{_ as i,o as t,c as n,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 454 | Dragon Ball · Quest Sediment Domain Review: Civilization Collapse Simulation After Goku's Absence","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 454 | Dragon Ball · Quest Sediment Domain Review: Civilization Collapse Simulation After Goku's Absence","no":454,"module":2,"tags":["Myriad-Realms Benchmark","Dragon Ball","Quest Sediment Domain Simulation","Civilization Collapse","Goku Absence","Single-Point Dependence"],"related":["21-Symbiotic Network Operating Principles","29-Symbiotic-Degree Assessment System","23-20% Activation Strategy Plan"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0454_模块2-龙珠-求索域复盘-悟空缺位后的文明崩溃模拟.md","filePath":"en/0454_模块2-龙珠-求索域复盘-悟空缺位后的文明崩溃模拟.md"}`),o={name:"en/0454_模块2-龙珠-求索域复盘-悟空缺位后的文明崩溃模拟.md"};function s(r,e,l,u,h,c){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="entry-454-dragon-ball-·-quest-sediment-domain-review-civilization-collapse-simulation-after-goku-s-absence" tabindex="-1">Entry 454 | Dragon Ball · Quest Sediment Domain Review: Civilization Collapse Simulation After Goku&#39;s Absence <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-454-dragon-ball-·-quest-sediment-domain-review-civilization-collapse-simulation-after-goku-s-absence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 454 | Dragon Ball · Quest Sediment Domain Review: Civilization Collapse Simulation After Goku&#39;s Absence&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Dragon Ball Full Decomposition (Entry 23 · Alternative 3) | Benchmark base: Documents 21, 29, 23</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-what-happens-when-goku-is-taken-off-the-chessboard" tabindex="-1">Introduction: what happens when Goku is taken off the chessboard? <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-what-happens-when-goku-is-taken-off-the-chessboard" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: what happens when Goku is taken off the chessboard?&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s Quest Sediment Domain simulation review is the ultimate tool to test a civilization&#39;s &quot;single-point dependence&quot;: take the protagonist off the chessboard, see how long civilization can go. Dragon Ball world&#39;s answer will be very cruel — if Goku truly died in the Cell arc, truly stayed in Other World not returning, how many more years can Earth hold? This entry takes the <strong>law-first axiom</strong> as core, giving Quest Sediment Domain&#39;s review report on Dragon Ball world.</p><p>This entry&#39;s judging base is the six top-level axioms and five mandatory cores, with the law-first axiom as core. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones-simulation-premise" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones (Simulation Premise) <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones-simulation-premise" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones (Simulation Premise)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Quest Sediment Domain simulation&#39;s premise is: Dragon Ball world&#39;s energy all hangs on Goku alone. Concrete manifestations:</p><ul><li>Earth&#39;s strongest warriors = Goku + Vegeta (Vegeta chased decades barely tied)</li><li>Ki theory not public; Earth cultivators&#39; highest combat power = Gohan/Piccolo level</li><li>God-tier stratum (God of Destruction/Angels/Zeno) does not intervene in Earth daily affairs</li><li>Dragon Ball wishing mechanism = the only &quot;rollback&quot; tool, but someone must gather seven balls</li></ul><p>On this premise, take Goku off the chessboard.</p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression-simulation-results" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression (Simulation Results) <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression-simulation-results" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression (Simulation Results)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Quest Sediment Domain replicates Dragon Ball world, injects &quot;Goku dies in Cell arc and stays in Other World not returning&quot; variable; observation results:</p><ol><li><strong>Stage 1 (years 1–5)</strong>: Vegeta alone holds the line; Gohan, Piccolo assist. Earth can handle general threats, but will struggle against the next cosmos-tier villain (e.g., Buu)</li><li><strong>Stage 2 (years 5–20)</strong>: Buu revives; Vegeta&#39;s self-destruction cannot stop him. Earth has no Goku&#39;s SSJ3/Super Saiyan God; Buu&#39;s probability of destroying Earth &gt; 90%</li><li><strong>Stage 3 (20+ years)</strong>: even if relying on Vegeta + Gohan + wish revival to survive Buu, the next wave of threats (e.g., Frieza revival, Zamasu) still no one can stop</li><li><strong>Conclusion</strong>: after Goku&#39;s absence, Earth civilization&#39;s expected survival years &lt; 30</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking-simulation-insights" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking (Simulation Insights) <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking-simulation-insights" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking (Simulation Insights)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Simulation results reveal Goku&#39;s predatory thinking&#39;s true price:</p><ul><li><strong>&quot;Luckily Goku is here&quot; is a normal-state hallucination</strong>: readers lived for forty years in the hallucination &quot;Goku can always make it in time,&quot; but Quest Sediment Domain tears off this layer</li><li><strong>Vegeta&#39;s chase is fake chase</strong>: Vegeta chased decades, always &quot;second strongest,&quot; not &quot;can independently carry the world&quot; strong one</li><li><strong>Companions&#39; marginalization is institutional</strong>: Tien Shinhan, Yamcha, Krillin late become backdrop; not that they did not work hard, but the system gave them no road</li></ul><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dragon Ball Single-Point Dependence</th><th>Quest-Sediment-Domain Alternative</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Goku absent, Earth collapses in 30 years</td><td>Anchor Council + separation of powers; any individual absent does not affect operation</td></tr><tr><td>Vegeta fake chase</td><td>20% activation strategy: strong ones emerge in batches; not by &quot;chasing Goku&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>Companions marginalized</td><td>300 Origin cultivation systems fully open; every cultivator has their own track</td></tr><tr><td>Disasters by wish rollback</td><td>Alaya Network + civilization-tier early warning; disasters have institutional response</td></tr><tr><td>God-tier stratum does not intervene</td><td>Causal self-discipline axiom: strong ones seeing Myriad Ranks&#39; suffering must observe first then limited interference</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: Quest Sediment Domain fully replicates Dragon Ball world&#39;s law parameters</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: stage injection &quot;Goku absent 10 years,&quot; &quot;absent 50 years,&quot; &quot;absent 100 years&quot;</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: count Earth civilization survival years, Myriad-Ranks casualty rate, Namek reconstruction rate</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: output <em>Dragon Ball Civilization Collapse Timeline After Goku Absence</em>, quantifying single-point dependence&#39;s civilizational price</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Simulation results&#39; insight on self-consistency</strong>: Dragon Ball world&#39;s &quot;peace&quot; was never institutional product, but Goku-present result — this itself is low-self-consistency manifestation</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk</strong>: GT turns Goku back into a child, Super brings Goku back to Earth, Heroes makes Goku cross time; essentially all are &quot;writers dare not let Goku truly absent&quot;</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency</strong>: high (gift-style-leaning-oligarchic) — Quest Sediment Domain simulation confirms this rating</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: Goku&#39;s energy not institutionalized; absent = collapse</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: companions&#39; marginalization is institutional, not that they did not work hard</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo absent, Peerless Academy still stands; Goku absent, Earth collapses in 30 years — Dragon Ball&#39;s single-point dependence is more severe than Tang Luo&#39;s</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: Myriad Ranks under Goku absence have no self-organization ability at all</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: Dragon Ball world cannot expand under Goku absence; can only circle in the loop &quot;Goku came back again&quot;</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power inherent in all; easygoing retain guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin eliminates predation motive</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Quest Sediment Domain&#39;s review result is cruel: Dragon Ball world is not a civilization, it is &quot;Goku&#39;s protective shield.&quot; Shield present, Earth present; shield gone, Earth gone. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s answer is not to make Goku stronger, but to make Earth no longer need Goku alone to get strong. Change &quot;luckily Goku is here&quot; to &quot;luckily we built institutions,&quot; and Dragon Ball world counts as truly mature.</p><p>In the final analysis, Dragon Ball · Quest Sediment Domain review · civilization collapse simulation after Goku&#39;s absence described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./453_模块2-龙珠-境界体系替代-九境加二境的稳定框架.html">Entry 453 · Realm-System Alternative</a> · <a href="./455_模块2-龙珠-制度替代收益-锚点共生注入龙珠世界.html">Entry 455 · Institutional-Alternative Benefits</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/21-共生网络运作原理.html">21-Symbiotic Network Operating Principles</a></li></ul>',29)])])}const m=i(o,[["render",s]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
